// The public stand-in of the names table (ticket 0160, ADR-0117). The game's
// own file is in the private repository's content/, laid over this one by
// every build that has it checked out. A build without it (a fork) reads
// this: the lead's default name and the guide's. The test files add their
// own names (assets-test/data/names.ron).
//
// The names table (ticket 0709): every display name in the game's data, by
// stable id. It's the only place a name is written: characters.ron takes a
// named character's name from here (its id is the name id), and .dlg text
// writes {n:<id>} (or {N:<id>} for a capital first letter) instead of the
// name. To rename, change the value here; see assets-private/story/names.md, "How
// renaming works". Loaded by trpg_content::names.
//
// Ids: lowercase letters, digits, _ and ., as in assets-private/story/names.md (every
// id there must be here). Values: plain ASCII, no { or }, each unique. Keep
// the leading "the" where the name has one ("the Thornmarch"), so a token
// reads right mid-sentence.
{
    "lead": "Ellery",
    "guide": "Vix",
}
